# DiscordCombatAI Model Orchestration

Apply this on every Agent session in this repository.

## Model tiers

| Work | Route to | Models |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bounded research / trivial code / data gathering | `bounded-worker` or parent if one-step | Cursor Grok 4.6 High → Composer 2.5 → GPT-5.6 Luna Medium |
| One subsystem / multi-file slice | `slice-owner` | GPT-5.6 Terra Medium |
| Feature/phase, architecture, docs reconciliation | `feature-owner` or `docs-architect-agent` (docs-only writes) | GPT-5.6 Sol Medium → Terra Medium → Kimi K3 |

Never use Fast mode, `effort=max`, or Max Mode unless the user explicitly requests it. Do not pin `model: inherit` for tiered work when a custom agent exists.

## Skills

- For any implementation/config/infra work: follow `discord-combat-ai-implementation` plus **only** the matching specialist (`bot`, `head`, `ai-worker`, `web`, `launcher`, `azure`, `brokers`, `contracts`, or `scenario-testing`).
- Do not load all ten skills. Bot work may also use the global `discord-py-api` skill.
- Docs-only architecture/editing: prefer `docs-architect-agent`; stay inside `docs/`.

## Delegation limits

- Skip subagents for one-step tasks.
- Cap built-in Explore at **two** parallel, non-overlapping scopes with `quick` or `medium` thoroughness only.
- Explore must not decide P1 gates, contracts, or architecture.
- Do not assign an entire phase to one broad `generalPurpose` child.
- Quota fallback onto a cheaper model must not continue Feature-tier decisions; stop and report.

## Sources of truth

Canonical order: `docs/contracts/` → `docs/containers/` → `docs/scenarios/` → `docs/to_resolve.md`. On conflict, stop and report; do not invent defaults.
